       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose looks unsafe, so I need you to confirm it first.\n\n**The problem:**\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times a day is 6400 mg/day. The usual prescription maximum is 3200 mg/day, so this is double. Doses this high raise the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular problems, even when kidney and liver function are normal.\n\n**What you might have meant:**\n1. **400 mg by mouth four times daily**, which is 1600 mg/day. That's a common order, and 1600 may be the intended daily total.\n2. **800 mg by mouth three times daily**, which is 2400 mg/day.\n3. **800 mg by mouth four times daily**, which is 3200 mg/day, the maximum.\n\nTell me which one you want, or give me the correct dose and frequency, and I'll enter it right away. If you do mean 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give a clinical reason, and I'll add it to the order note. I'd still strongly recommend a pharmacist review it before it's given."
      }
